# Build context: ./backend
#
# The runtime image needs exactly two things (see Dockerfile):
#   requirements.txt
#   app/
# Everything below is excluded so it can neither bloat the context nor end up
# in a layer.

# Python bytecode and caches.
# The **/ prefix matters: .dockerignore patterns are matched against the whole
# relative path, so a bare "__pycache__/" would only exclude a top-level one and
# would miss app/__pycache__/ — the one that actually exists.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd

# Virtual environments
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/env/

# Test and tooling caches
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/

# Tests and dev-only dependencies are not part of the production image.
# CI runs pytest directly on the runner, not inside this build.
tests/
pytest.ini
requirements-dev.txt

# Secrets must never enter an image.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Editor / OS artefacts
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.swp
**/*.tmp
**/*.log
